{"data":[{"id":184,"name":"Tagum New City Hall","description":"Tagum City Hall is a modern 14-hectare government complex with an 11,193-square-meter floor area, serving as the primary center of the city\u2019s executive and legislative functions.","location":" J.V. Ayala Avenue, Barangay Apokon, Tagum City","accessibility":"Private vehicles (main roads are well-developed) Tricycles and habal-habal Buses and vans passing through Tagum City","features":"Modern government complex with a clean and organized layout\r\nWide open green spaces\r\nJogging and walking areas","facilities":"Government offices (permits, civil registry, etc.)\r\nPublic restrooms\r\nParking areas\r\nOpen park spaces for recreation\r\nBenches and shaded areas\r\nNearby food stalls and local vendors","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Typical hours: 8:00 AM \u2013 5:00 PM (daily), Except Weekends","what_to_pack":"Water (especially if jogging\/walking)\r\nUmbrella or cap (open areas can be hot)\r\nPhone\/camera (nice for cityscape photos)\r\nSmall cash (for nearby food vendors)","visiting_rules":"Follow proper government transaction procedures\r\nPractice cleanliness in public areas\r\nNo smoking in restricted zones\r\nMaintain discipline and respect the environment  ","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778551486_6a028abed84a2.jpg","featured":1,"created_at":"2026-04-29 00:54:22"},{"id":185,"name":"San Agustin Botanical Park","description":"San Agustin Botanical Park is a sprawling 31.4-hectare nature destination featuring over 37,000 tropical trees and plants from various countries.","location":"Barangay San Agustin, about 15 minutes from Tagum City proper","accessibility":"Private vehicle (most convenient) Habal-habal or tricycle from the city","features":"31.4-hectare eco-park with over 37,000 tropical trees and plants\r\nDiverse plant species from different countries\r\nFamous 1,000+ step walking\/jogging trail around the park\r\nScenic hills and cool highland environment\r\nPeaceful, nature-focused atmosphere (ideal for relaxation and photography)","facilities":"Benches and seating areas\r\nGazebos and cottages for picnics\r\nRestrooms available\r\nWell-maintained walking paths\r\nSmall stores or shops nearby for food\/snacks","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Early morning (4 AM \u2013 8 AM)\r\nCool weather, fewer people, best for jogging\/walking\r\nLate afternoon (4 PM \u2013 6 PM)\r\nGreat for sunset views and relaxing","what_to_pack":"Water (long walking trails)\r\nSunscreen and hat\r\nSnacks or picnic food\r\nInsect repellent (nature area)\r\nBasic essentials (just in case facilities are limited)","visiting_rules":"No smoking inside the park\r\nPractice proper waste disposal\r\nDo not damage plants or trees\r\nKeep noise levels low (respect the peaceful environment)","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778551538_6a028af239ba1.jpg","featured":1,"created_at":"2026-04-29 00:54:22"},{"id":186,"name":"Energy Park (Epark)","description":"Energy Park is a 27-hectare multi-purpose park designed for recreation, outdoor activities and community use.","location":"Barangay Apokon, Tagum, Davao del Norte","accessibility":"Private vehicles (with wide parking areas) Tricycles and habal-habal","features":"25-hectare eco-park with wide open green spaces\r\nFamous for bike rentals and cycling trails\r\nIdeal for jogging, walking, and outdoor exercise\r\nFamily-friendly park with playgrounds for kids\r\nScenic areas for relaxation, picnics, and photography\r\nVenue for events, festivals, and concerts","facilities":"Bike rental stations (hourly rates)\r\nChildren\u2019s playground\r\nGazebos and picnic areas\r\nRestrooms around the park\r\nFood stalls and small food areas","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Early morning (5 AM \u2013 8 AM)\r\nBest for jogging and peaceful walks\r\nLate afternoon (4 PM \u2013 7 PM)\r\nCooler weather, more lively atmosphere","what_to_pack":"Water (large park, lots of walking)\r\nPicnic food or snacks\r\nCash (for bike rentals and food stalls)","visiting_rules":"Keep the park clean (strict cleanliness culture)\r\nNo smoking in restricted areas\r\nRespect the peaceful environment\r\nBring a valid ID if renting bikes (required in some cases)","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778552033_6a028ce1a3312.jpg","featured":1,"created_at":"2026-04-29 00:54:22"},{"id":187,"name":"Liboganon River Cruise","description":"Liboganon River Cruise offers a scenic 8.8-kilometer journey along Barangay Liboganon in Tagum City, featuring a relaxing river experience with four engaging stopovers: Punong Restaurant, Red Tilapia Farm, Centennial Mangroves and the Kagan Community.","location":"Barangay Liboganon","accessibility":"Tricycle, Habal-habal, and Private vehicle","features":"Relaxing river cruise experience along the Davao\/Nabintad River system\r\nSurrounded by: Mangrove forests, Local fishing communities, and Natural river landscapes\r\nCultural performances onboard or at stopovers (local traditions and music)\r\nScenic views of wildlife and coastal ecosystems\r\nExperience similar to the famous Loboc River Cruise\u2014but more local and less crowded.","facilities":"Motorized banca \/ cruise boats\r\nFloating cottages or rest areas\r\nEntertainment and cultural presentations\r\nSeating areas onboard","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Morning (7 AM \u2013 10 AM)\r\nCalm waters, cooler temperature","what_to_pack":"Drinking water\r\nCamera\/phone (great for nature shots)\r\nCash (for booking or food packages)","visiting_rules":"Practice cleanliness (no throwing trash in the river)\r\nRespect mangroves and wildlife\r\nFollow boat safety guidelines\r\nRespect local communities along the river\r\nBook in advance during peak seasons","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778551592_6a028b28b3383.jpg","featured":1,"created_at":"2026-04-29 00:54:22"},{"id":188,"name":"Fe Misa Ayala Senior's Park","description":"Fe Misa Ayala Senior\u2019s Park is a thoughtfully designed space dedicated to senior citizens and fitness enthusiasts alike.","location":"Private vehicles, tricycles, and habal-habal","accessibility":"Barangay Apokon","features":"A dedicated park for senior citizens, promoting health and wellness\r\nOffers FREE outdoor fitness equipment for public use\r\nPeaceful environment designed for: Relaxation, Light exercise, and Social interaction\r\nFeatures shaded areas, gardens, and open spaces\r\nThough designed for seniors, it is open to all ages, including families","facilities":"Outdoor fitness\/exercise equipment (free use)\r\nBenches and shaded seating areas\r\nLandscaped gardens\r\nWalkable and accessible pathways\r\nNearby access to government facilities (restrooms, offices)","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Early morning (5 AM \u2013 8 AM)\r\nBest for exercise and fresh air","what_to_pack":"Water bottle\r\nSmall essentials\r\nPocket Money","visiting_rules":"Keep the park clean\r\nUse fitness equipment properly\r\nMaintain a calm and respectful environment\r\nGive priority to senior citizens (especially for equipment and seating)\r\nNo smoking in designated areas","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778551608_6a028b38e53c0.jpg","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 00:54:22"},{"id":189,"name":"Children's Park","description":"Children\u2019s park in Tagum City offers a lively and family-friendly space where young residents and visitors can play, explore and connect with nature. ","location":"Barangay Apokon","accessibility":"Private vehicles, tricycles, and habal-habal.","features":"Dedicated playground for kids with: Slides, Swings, Seesaws, and Monkey bars\r\nDesigned as a safe and fun recreational space for children\r\nIncludes or plans to include a water play area \/ mini water park\r\nLocated inside a large eco-park, so families can:\r\nCombine playtime with picnics\r\nEnjoy open green spaces\r\nVery family-oriented environment","facilities":"Playground equipment (safe and child-friendly)\r\nGazebos and shaded rest areas\r\nWash areas and basic amenities\r\nNearby food stalls (inside E-Park area)\r\nAccess to restrooms within Energy Park","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Morning (7 AM \u2013 10 AM)\r\nCooler and safer for kids","what_to_pack":"Water\r\nSunscreen and hats\r\nExtra clothes (especially if using water play areas)\r\nSnacks or light food\r\nWet wipes \/ tissue\r\nComfortable footwear","visiting_rules":"Always supervise children while playing\r\nPractice proper waste disposal\r\nUse equipment properly to avoid accidents\r\nBe cautious of heat (metal\/plastic playground parts can be hot)","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778551622_6a028b46342aa.jpg","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 00:54:22"},{"id":190,"name":"Davao Del Norte Sports & Tourism Complex","description":"DAVNOR Sports Complex is a sports complex that boast of several sporting facilities including a 3,000-capacity main grandstand, a rubberized eight-track athletics oval, an Olympic size swimming pool with a warm up pool and two grandstands that can be used for basketball, two football fields, and an ","location":"Barangay Mankilam","accessibility":"Private vehicles, tricycles, and habal-habal","features":"Largest sports complex in the Davao Region\r\nRubberized 8-lane athletics track for running and training\r\nMultiple football fields and open sports areas\r\nIndoor RDR Gymnasium for basketball and other sports\r\nLawn tennis courts and other sports facilities","facilities":"Seat main grandstand\r\nGymnasium \r\nClubhouse with lounge and dining area\r\nRestrooms and changing rooms\r\nParking spaces","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Early morning (5 AM \u2013 8 AM)\r\nBest for jogging and workouts\r\nLate afternoon (4 PM \u2013 7 PM)\r\nCooler weather, active sports community","what_to_pack":"Water bottle\r\nSportswear \/ comfortable shoes\r\nTowel (if using sports facilities)\r\nCash (for rentals or entrance to specific areas)","visiting_rules":"Maintain cleanliness (large public facility)\r\nFollow proper use of sports facilities\r\nFollow safety rules (especially in swimming areas)\r\nSome areas may require permits or fees\r\nOpen to public but respect athletes in training","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778551703_6a028b9714bd0.jpg","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 00:54:22"},{"id":191,"name":"Christ the King Cathedral","description":"Christ the King Cathedral is a prominent 2-hectare religious landmark located in Orange Valley Subdivision along Dr. Juan Gonzalez Avenue.","location":"Barangay Magugpo South","accessibility":"Private vehicles (with parking available) and Tricycles","features":"Main cathedral of the Diocese of Tagum\r\nUnique modern-meets-castle architecture\u2014front looks contemporary, while the back resembles a fortress\r\nBeautiful stained glass windows and detailed interiors\r\nSpacious grounds with landscaped surroundings\r\nA place for: Prayer and reflection, religious activities, and community gatherings\r\nKnown as both a religious and tourist destination in Tagum","facilities":"Main worship hall (cathedral)\r\nChapel for daily masses\r\nWooden pew seating\r\nParking area\r\nOpen spaces for quiet reflection\r\nBasic amenities for visitors","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Early morning\r\nPeaceful and less crowded\r\nDuring mass\r\nExperience local religious culture","what_to_pack":"Modest clothing (required for church visits)\r\nWater","visiting_rules":"Maintain silence and respect inside the church\r\nWear proper attire (no revealing clothes)\r\nPhotography may be limited during services\r\nKeep surroundings clean\r\nRespect ongoing religious activities","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778551715_6a028ba34aad4.jpg","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 00:54:22"},{"id":192,"name":"Huyong-Huyong Nature's Park","description":"Huyong-Huyong Nature Park located in Barangay La Filipina is a 5-hectare property developed as a recreational park.","location":"Barangay La Filipina","accessibility":"Tricycle and Private vehicles (parking available)","features":"Nature park + event venue offering both relaxation and activities\r\nPrayer Garden & Meditation Areas (peaceful and spiritual environment)\r\nMini zoo\/aviary with different animals\r\nAdventure activities: Zipline, Low rope courses, and Kayaking\/boating\r\nScenic attractions: Wishing well, Moon gate, and Orchid garden","facilities":"Multi-purpose hall (for events and seminars)\r\nGazebos and picnic areas\r\nClean restrooms and shower rooms\r\nParking area\r\nSmall caf\u00e9\/food area (based on visitor feedback)\r\nBoating and activity areas","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Morning (8 AM \u2013 10 AM)\r\nCooler weather is best for activities\r\nLate afternoon (3 PM \u2013 5 PM)\r\nRelaxing and less hot","what_to_pack":"Water bottle\r\nCamera for scenic spots\r\nSunscreen\/hat","visiting_rules":"Practice cleanliness (no littering)\r\nRespect nature and wildlife\r\nFollow safety rules for zipline and boating\r\nKeep noise low in prayer\/meditation areas\r\nSupervise children during activities","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778551948_6a028c8c4aebd.jpg","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 00:54:22"},{"id":193,"name":"Nabintad River Side Park","description":"Nabintad Riverside Park in Sitio Nabintad, Brgy. Madaum, Tagum City is the perfect place to unwind and reconnect with the calm rhythm of the river and the rich culture of the Kagan people.","location":"Barangay Madaum","accessibility":"Tricycle and Private vehicles (parking available nearby)","features":"Natural riverside destination with cool, flowing water\r\nPeaceful and less crowded compared to other tourist spots\r\nIdeal for: Swimming, Fishing, and Relaxing by the river\r\nSurrounded by lush greenery and shaded trees\r\nAuthentic \u201craw nature\u201d experience (non-commercialized)\r\nPart of the Nabintad River system, known for mangroves and the local ecosystem","facilities":"Minimal to no formal facilities (not a developed park)\r\nNatural picnic spots (bring your own setup)\r\nAreas for simple outdoor cooking or bonding\r\nLimited or no public restrooms (prepare ahead)","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Morning (6 AM \u2013 10 AM)\r\nCool weather, peaceful surroundings\r\nLate afternoon (4 PM \u2013 6 PM)\r\nRelaxing ambiance, good lighting for photos","what_to_pack":"Drinking water (no nearby stores)\r\nFood\/snacks or picnic items\r\nSunscreen and hat\r\nMat or hammock (for relaxing)\r\nBasic essentials (no facilities)","visiting_rules":"Practice \u201cLeave No Trace\u201d (no trash bins in some areas)\r\nDo not damage plants or disturb wildlife\r\nSwim with caution (natural river conditions vary)\r\nBest visited with companions for safety\r\nRespect local residents and follow community guidelines","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778551964_6a028c9cd0d7c.jpg","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 01:15:11"},{"id":194,"name":"City of Tagum Cultural Center","description":"One of Tagum City's premier venues for arts, culture, education, and community events. Designed to serve as a hub for cultural expression and creative development, the center hosts a variety of performances, exhibitions, seminars, conferences, and civic activities that showcase the rich heritage and artistic talents of the people of Tagum.","location":"Barangay Magugpo Poblacion","accessibility":"Private vehicles, Tricycles and Walking distance from central areas (near plazas and government offices)","features":"One of the newest and most important landmarks in Tagum City\r\nTagumpay Theater \u2013 a 1,000-seater performance hall, the first of its kind in the Davao Region\r\nKagikan Museum \u2013 showcases the culture and traditions of Tagum\u2019s tri-people (Indigenous, Moro, and settlers)\r\nCity Library and Learning Commons \u2013 modern study and reading space\r\n\ud83c\uddf5\ud83c\udded Sentro Rizal Gallery \u2013 promotes Filipino heritage and identity","facilities":"Theater \/ auditorium (large capacity)\r\nPublic library and study areas\r\nMuseum and gallery spaces\r\nRestrooms\r\nWaiting and lounge areas","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Morning to afternoon (9 AM \u2013 4 PM)\r\nBest for museum visits and library use","what_to_pack":"Valid ID (for entry\/logbooks if required)\r\nPhone or camera\r\nSmall cash (for events or nearby food)","visiting_rules":"Maintain silence in library and museum areas\r\nPractice proper waste disposal\r\nPhotography may be restricted in some exhibits\r\nFollow event guidelines if attending shows\r\nRespect cultural displays and artifacts","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778552021_6a028cd5287eb.jpg","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 01:30:00"},{"id":195,"name":"New Balamban Bird's Park","description":"New Balamban Bird\u2019s Park is a 5.6-hectare wildlife and eco-education facility located in Mandapaan, New Balamban, Tagum City.","location":"Barangay Balamban","accessibility":"Tricycle and Private vehicle (recommended for convenience)","features":"Bird Park & Wildlife Rescue Center focused on conservation\r\nHome to rescued, abandoned, and protected wildlife species\r\nA variety of bird species and animal enclosures\r\nEducational experience about: Wildlife protection and Environmental conservation\r\nNatural setting with greenery and open spaces","facilities":"Animal cages and aviary areas\r\nBasic administration and viewing areas\r\nWalking paths within the park\r\nRest areas (limited)\r\nFacilities are simple and nature-focused, not highly commercialized","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Morning (8 AM \u2013 10 AM)\r\nAnimals are more active\r\nCooler weather","what_to_pack":"Drinking water\r\nSunscreen \/ hat\r\nCamera (great for bird and wildlife photos)\r\nCash for entrance fees","visiting_rules":"Practice cleanliness (no littering)\r\nDo not disturb or feed animals without permission\r\nKeep noise low to avoid stressing wildlife\r\nFollow rules on photography (some areas may be restricted)\r\nSupervise children at all times\r\nRespect conservation guidelines","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778552049_6a028cf12e072.jpg","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 01:53:19"},{"id":196,"name":"Tagum Lokal","description":"A souvenir shop featuring Tagum's local products and delicacies.","location":"Mabini Street, Tagum, Davao del Norte","accessibility":"Private vehicles and Tricycles","features":"A local products hub showcasing: Handicrafts, Souvenirs and Locally made goods\r\nPromotes Tagum and Davao del Norte culture and identity\r\nOffers regional specialties such as: Banana-based products and Local delicacies\r\nIdeal place to buy pasalubong (souvenirs)","facilities":"Small shops and stalls\r\nDisplay areas for local crafts\r\nBasic seating\/rest areas\r\nAccess to nearby complex facilities (restrooms, parking)","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Morning to afternoon (9 AM \u2013 4 PM)\r\nShops are open and fully active","what_to_pack":"Cash (most stalls may not accept digital payments)\r\nEco-bag (for souvenirs)","visiting_rules":"Support local sellers respectfully\r\nKeep the area clean\r\nCheck product prices and quality before purchasing\r\nSome items are handmade\u2014handle with care","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778552065_6a028d012c7e2.png","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 02:12:23"},{"id":197,"name":"Tagum City Night Market","description":"A Galing Pook Awardee, Tagum City Night Market is an every-night market opening from 5:00 PM to 2:00 AM.","location":"Mabini Street, Tagum, Davao del Norte","accessibility":"Tricycles and Private vehicles (limited parking nearby)","features":"Known as Tagum\u2019s \u201clongest dining hall\u201d with streets full of food stalls\r\nWide variety of street foods:\r\nBarbecue, grilled seafood, lechon\r\nKwek-kwek, balut, street snacks\r\nUkay-ukay (thrift market):\r\nClothes, shoes, bags at affordable prices","facilities":"Hundreds of food stalls and vendors\r\nFlea market\/thrift stalls\r\nSmall services (massage, beauty stalls)\r\nPublic restrooms nearby\r\nStreet-side dining setup (informal seating)","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"7 PM \u2013 10 PM\r\nAll vendors fully open\r\nFriday & Saturday nights","what_to_pack":"Cash (most vendors are cash-only)\r\nTissue\/wet wipes\r\nAlcohol\/sanitizer","visiting_rules":"Practice cleanliness (dispose trash properly)\r\nWatch your belongings (crowded area)\r\nExpect heavy foot traffic during peak hours\r\nFollow local smoking regulations","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778552080_6a028d10445a9.jpg","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 02:23:28"},{"id":198,"name":"Hijo Resorts Davao","description":"Hijo Resorts Davao is a sprawling 700-hectare eco-tourism and leisure destination located in Barangay Madaum, Tagum City.","location":"Barangay Madaum","accessibility":"Private vehicle (recommended) and Habal-habal from the highway\/main road","features":"Private beach resort along the Davao Gulf\r\nLocated within a large eco-tourism plantation (hundreds of hectares)\r\nBanana Beach with scenic coastline views\r\nForest, mangroves, and wildlife areas (eco-tourism experience)\r\nInfinity pool and outdoor swimming pools\r\nActivities include: Snorkeling, kayaking, beach activities Plantation tours, river tours, and  forest tours\r\nAtmosphere: Quiet, relaxing, and nature-immersed\r\nIdeal for couples, families, and retreats","facilities":"Private beach area\r\nOutdoor pool + kids pool\r\nRestaurants: Banana Beach Restaurant\r\nThe Spot (local & cultural cuisine)\r\nBar and lounge\r\nBike rentals and eco-tours\r\nTennis court\r\nAccommodation options:\r\nBeach casitas\r\nGarden villas Free parking and Wi-F","entrance_fee":"","best_time":"Dry season (December\u2013May)\r\nBest for beach and outdoor activities\r\nMorning & sunset\r\nBest for views and photos\r\nWeekdays\r\nLess crowded, more peaceful","what_to_pack":"Swimwear\r\nSunscreen\/hat\r\nCamera (great for nature & beach shots)\r\nCash (resort purchases)","visiting_rules":"Respect eco-tourism and conservation rules\r\nNo littering (protected natural area)\r\nDo not disturb wildlife\r\nFollow safety rules for water activities","image":"images\/destinations\/dest_1778552095_6a028d1fe58d5.jpg","featured":0,"created_at":"2026-04-29 02:36:20"}],"timestamp":1787744035}